# Docker build context — allowlist ("fail closed")
#
# Rules here are the single most security-sensitive file in the repo: this file
# decides what leaves the developer's machine. `.gitignore` is NOT consulted by
# Docker, so without it every `docker build` would ship the whole working tree.
#
# Measured on the repo as of 2026-10-01, a denyless build context is ~264 MB and
# includes `.env` (MISTRAL_API_KEY, the Neon URL, the Kinde issuer), `.venv`
# (258 MB) and `.git`. That is the failure this file exists to prevent.
#
# Strategy: exclude everything, then re-include only the handful of paths the
# image build actually reads. A newly added secret is therefore excluded by
# default, instead of being exposed because someone forgot to extend a denylist.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WARNING — Docker's .dockerignore has NO inline-comment syntax.
# A `#` only starts a comment as the FIRST character of a line. Trailing text
# after a pattern becomes part of the pattern itself, so
#
#     !pyproject.toml    # the deps file
#
# parses as the pattern "!pyproject.toml    # the deps file", matches nothing,
# and the re-include silently fails (context ships empty). Every comment in this
# file is therefore on its own line. Do not "tidy" them into trailing form.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Exclude every top-level entry by default.
*

# --- build inputs -----------------------------------------------------------
# deps, build backend, and [tool.hatch.build] packages
!pyproject.toml
# required by `uv sync --frozen`
!uv.lock
# pyproject sets readme = "README.md"; hatchling reads it during the wheel build
!README.md
# the package itself. src/app/prompts/ is a module inside src/ and IS needed.
!src/

# --- keep build outputs clean ----------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
**/.DS_Store
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# --- belt-and-braces ---------------------------------------------------------
# Already excluded by the allowlist above; restated so an accidental future
# re-include can't quietly pull one of these back into the context.
#
# These are deliberately root-anchored (leading "/"). Do NOT "simplify" them to
# `**/prompts` or `**/tests`: those would also match src/app/prompts/ and tests/
# and silently break the build.
/.env
/.env.*
/.venv
/.git
# LangGraph sqlite scratch
/store
/sandbox
/prototype
/notebooks
# prototype-only placeholder; the real prompts are src/app/prompts
/prompts
# runtime image must not migrate Prisma's schema
/alembic
/alembic.ini
/tests
/_markdown
/_nextjs_repo_context
/Dockerfile

# `.python-version` (3.14.6) is intentionally NOT shipped. The base image floats
# on the 3.14 line, so pinning an exact patch here would make uv try to download
# its own interpreter mid-build. Excluding it lets uv resolve against the image's
# system python via `requires-python = ">=3.14.6"`; WS9.2 pairs this with
# UV_PYTHON_DOWNLOADS=never so that resolution can never reach the network.
/.python-version